      <p>Beyond these, our <a href="/blog/nvme-vps-under-10-2026/" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">NVMe VPS under $10</a> and <a href="/blog/2026-black-friday-cheap-vps-under-25/" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">Black Friday cheap VPS</a> roundups are the best places to watch for promo-locked rates that survive the crunch.</p>

      <h2 id="migration-playbook" class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4">Locking in Your Rate: Smart Migration Playbook</h2>
      <p>If you decide to move (or just want to lock a low rate before the next wave), do it the disciplined way:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Prepay annually during promo windows.</strong> Annual prepay is the single most effective way to freeze a rate for a year. Catch a promo at the start of a billing cycle and you've hedged against any Q3/Q4 repricing.</li>
        <li><strong>Use a locked-rate host for the term.</strong> A provider with a fixed annual price — <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">RackNerd's annual deals are the standing example</a> — means no renewal surprise for the whole term.</li>
        <li><strong>Spin up a second, low-cost box to test migration.</strong> Deploy your stack on the new host, run your real workload for a few days, and confirm performance before you commit.</li>
        <li><strong>Plan the DNS/data migration order.</strong> Export databases and configs, lower the TTL on your DNS records before the cutover, then repoint.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep the old host up until the new one is proven.</strong> Classic mistake: killing the old box before the new one is verified. Run them in parallel for a day, then decommission.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Two timing notes that save real money in a price-wave year. First, <strong>stagger your lock-ins.</strong> If you run several boxes, don't renew them all in the same quarter — space annual renewals across the year so a single repricing event can't raise every bill at once, and you always have a clean window to migrate one box without touching the others. Second, <strong>watch the promo cycle, not the calendar.</strong> The largest fixed-rate deals in this market still cluster around seasonal windows; our <a href="/blog/2026-black-friday-cheap-vps-under-25/" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400">Black Friday cheap VPS roundup</a> is where the biggest locked-rate offers get catalogued each cycle. Catching one of those and prepaying a year keeps your effective rate well below a mid-wave renewal.</p>
